3. In accordance with Article IV of the 1958 New York Convention, an application to a Chinese court for recognition and enforcement of an arbitral award made in the territory of another Contracting State shall be submitted by one party to the arbitral award. An application by a party shall be accepted by the intermediate people's court at the following locations in China:
(1) where the party against whom enforcement is sought is a natural person, the place of his/her domicile or habitual residence;
(2) where the party against whom enforcement is sought is a legal person, the place of its principal office;
(3) where the party against whom enforcement is sought has no domicile, habitual residence, or principal office in China but has property within China, the place where the property is located.
